.TH WERKMEISTER-CLOSE-OUT 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-close\-out \- End a workspace. After every PR shipped: close the issue, write closeout.md, remove the workspace, delete merged branches. With \-\-abandon: record the reason, push every branch and keep them, remove the workspace. Refuses without postmortem.md (run the post\-mortem first) unless \-\-skip\-postmortem gives a reason
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister close\-out\fR [name]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-abandon <reason>\fR
Close out without shipping; the reason goes in closeout.md and the PR files
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-postmortem <reason>\fR
Close out without a post\-mortem; the reason goes in closeout.md
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The one way to end a workspace. First the post\-mortem: it refuses without \fBpostmortem.md\fR unless \fB\-\-skip\-postmortem\fR gives a reason. After every PR shipped, it closes the issue, writes \fBcloseout.md\fR, removes the workspace and deletes merged branches. With \fB\-\-abandon\fR and a reason, it records the reason, leaves the issue, pushes every branch and keeps them, and removes the workspace. It lists terminal Claude sessions still open in the workspace.
.PP
The full process is in docs/workspace\-lifecycle.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister close\-out
werkmeister close\-out my\-feature \-\-abandon "superseded by SW\-200"
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
